      "title": "Manifest failure leaves a published bundle behind",
      "message": "package() publishes the final bundle before the manifest is written. If manifest directory creation or writing fails (for example, because of permissions or a full disk), the command fails but leaves the final .app behind, potentially alongside a truncated manifest. Retrying then fails because the output already exists. This violates the documented failure-cleanup guarantee.",
      "suggestion": "Stage the manifest in a temporary file before publishing the bundle, atomically replace the manifest, and roll back the newly published bundle if manifest publication fails. Keep both publication steps within the packaging transaction.",
